    "title": "How to Watch Texas vs Purdue: TV Channel, Stream, & Tip-Off Time",
    "text": "© 2026 SaturdayDownSouth.com Home > News > Sports > How to Watch Texas vs Purdue: TV Channel, Stream, & Tip-Off Time Ad Disclosure This article/post contains references to products or services from one or more of our advertisers or partners. We may receive compensation when you click on links to those products or services. The Texas Longhorns and the Purdue Boilermakers meet in a postseason matchup. Head coach Matt Painter leads a Purdue squad that holds a 27-8 overall record and a 2-0 standing in Big Ten postseason play. They face a challenge in head coach Sean Miller and his Texas team. The Longhorns enter this neutral-site game with a perfect 3-0 postseason standing in the SEC and an active three-game winning streak. Watch Texas vs Purdue on Paramount+. This game tests Purdue against a Texas roster carrying late-season momentum. For fans looking to follow the action, continue reading to find all the essential broadcast information. This includes the exact tip-off time, the arena location, the CBS television channel assignment, and available streaming options to watch the game live. When is Texas vs Purdue? What Time Does It Start? The postseason game between the Texas Longhorns and the Purdue Boilermakers is scheduled for March 26, 2026. Tip-off is set for 7:10 PM ET, which is 4:10 PM PT local time. Where is Texas vs Purdue? This matchup takes place at the SAP Center at San Jose, located in San Jose, California. Because this is a neutral-site event, the Purdue Boilermakers will act as the designated home team. The Texas Longhorns will serve as the designated away team for the contest. How Can I Watch Texas vs Purdue? The postseason matchup between the Texas Longhorns and the Purdue Boilermakers will broadcast on national television. Fans can watch the game live on CBS. The network will provide full coverage of the neutral-site contest leading up to the scheduled 7:10 PM ET tip-off. Viewers can check their local television listings to find the specific CBS channel in their area. How Can I Stream Texas vs Purdue? For fans preferring to stream the matchup, the CBS television broadcast is accessible through multiple digital platforms. Because CBS is the primary network for this game, the broadcast is available directly through a Paramount+. Subscribers can use the platform to stream their live local CBS feed. In addition to Paramount+, viewers without traditional cable can watch the game through live TV streaming services such as Fubo and Sling that carry CBS. These platforms include local broadcast options in their subscription packages. Viewers should verify that CBS is available in their specific media market on these services prior to tip-off. Game Preview: Who Will Win Texas vs Purdue? Data from Kalshi on March 24th. Based on the latest data from the Kalshi prediction market, Purdue is mathematically more likely to win this matchup. The forecasting platform gives the Boilermakers a 74% implied probability of securing the victory. Conversely, the Texas Longhorns enter the contest with a 26% implied probability of winning the game. The prediction market clearly establishes the Boilermakers as the favorite while positioning the Longhorns as the underdog. Creative Manager and Writer at Sportradar. Craig has previously worked as a camera operator and video director in radio and television, as well as a content coordinator in the non-profit sector. You might also like...",
